# Performance

Read `performance.md` before changing lists, Zustand stores, SQLite, background tasks, or LLM code.

- React Compiler is on. Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` / `React.memo` unless a profiled hot path needs it.
- Zustand: selector slices only. Never `useStore()`. Do not return a new object from a selector.
- Split `uiStore` (progress, toast, Refresh) from data stores. Do not write into list stores during inference. Throttle progress to 250ms.
- Lists (transactions, events, subscriptions, tasks): FlashList or virtualized FlatList. Never `ScrollView` + `.map`.
- `StyleSheet.create` at file bottom. No inline style objects on list rows.
- LLM runs in `react-native-executorch` or `llama.rn` on a dev build — never Expo Go, never the JS thread. Regex first, batch 10–20, hash-cache, unload after the window (6–9am, 12–1pm, 8–10pm + Refresh).
- `expo-sqlite` with indexes; batch writes; no `SELECT *` on Home. Settings via localStorage polyfill. No AsyncStorage, no Axios.
- Background work: `expo-background-task` / `expo-task-manager` only. Never log raw SMS or amounts.

```ts
// BAD
const all = useTransactionStore();
useTransactionStore((s) => ({ items: s.items }));

// GOOD
const items = useTransactionStore((s) => s.items);
```
